  "description": "TPO 301/2003 T4 and T5.\r\nT1 Small leaved lime - Tree has heavy lean over road and toward neighbouring properties. It is also leaning slightly on the boundary fence. Structurally the tree seems okay there are a few small cavities in the stem which are fairly historic. Trim all epicormic growth around the base up to 4 meters to allow for easy assessment of fungus & cavities. Due of the incline of the tree and the slight pressure on the fence, suggest heavy pollard to reduce windsale and excess weight growing at the angle. To reduce the height of the tree from 18m down to 10m. Spread from 5-4m T2 Adjacent Small leaved lime Reducing this tree in line with T1 to an even height so that they are balanced and not at risk of excess wind with just T1 being reduced. To match the height and spread of T1 From 18m height down to 10m From 6m spread down to 4m.",
